Article 3 Where personal injury to another person caused by high voltage electricity falls under any of the following circumstances, the owner of the electric power facility shall not bear civil liability:
(1) force majeure;
(2) the victim commits suicide or self-injury by means of electric shock;
(3) the victim steals electric energy, steals or damages electric power facilities, or causes an electric shock accident due to other criminal acts;
(4) the victim engages in acts prohibited by laws or administrative regulations within the protection area of electric power facilities.
